SUMMARY:🌅🌊 SUMMER EVENING WALK OF THE TORONTO ISLANDS (9KM) 🌊🌅
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n🌅🌊 SUMMER EVENING WALK OF TH
 E TORONTO ISLANDS (9KM) 🌊🌅\n\nSunset Views\, Island Paths & Toronto'
 s Best Skyline\nThere is something magical about the Toronto Islands in th
 e evening.\n\nAs the city begins to slow down\, the islands come alive wit
 h golden light\, cool lake breezes\, and some of the most spectacular view
 s in Toronto. It feels like you've escaped the city without ever leaving i
 t.\nJoin us for a relaxed summer evening walk across the T\n\nToronto Isla
 nds as we explore Hanlan's Point\, Centre Island\, and Ward's Island while
  enjoying beaches\, open green spaces\, charming cottages\, and breathtaki
 ng skyline views.\n\nThe Toronto Islands have a fascinating history. Origi
 nally connected to the mainland as a long sandbar peninsula\, a powerful s
 torm in 1858 permanently separated the land from Toronto\, creating the is
 lands we know today.\n\nOver the years they've been home to amusement park
 s\, summer cottages\, beaches\, and the unique island community that still
  exists today on Ward's Island.\n\nThis is not a formal historical tour.\n
 It's a social walk with beautiful scenery\, fresh air\, and great conversa
 tion.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ Click here to join](https://ch
 at.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n***\n\n🚶‍♂️ What We'll
  Do\n\nWe'll take the ferry together to Hanlan's Point and begin our walk 
 across the islands.\n\nOur route will take us through:\n🌊 Hanlan's Poin
 t\n🌳 Centre Island\n🏡 Ward's Island\n📸 Multiple skyline viewpoint
 s\n🏖️ Beaches and waterfront paths\n\nWe'll stop throughout the eveni
 ng to enjoy the scenery\, take photos\, and soak in one of Toronto's most 
 beautiful summer experiences.\nAs the sun begins to set\, we'll enjoy some
  of the best views of the city skyline anywhere in Toronto.\n\nFeel free t
 o bring a snack or something small to share.\nYou're welcome to leave at a
 ny time or stay and explore after the walk.\n\n***\n\n☀️ Weather & Exp
 ectations\n\nThis event will happen in typical summer weather conditions.\
 nThat means warm temperatures\, sunshine\, clouds\, or light rain.\nThe is
 lands are often cooler and breezier than downtown Toronto\, especially lat
 er in the evening\, so bringing a light sweater or jacket is recommended.\
 n\nThe only reason we would cancel is for severe weather or thunderstorms.
 \n\nAlso — this is NOT a guided historical tour. I'll share bits of hist
 ory throughout the walk\, but the focus is social connection and enjoying 
 the islands together.\n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup Details\n📍 Meetup Location:
  Inside the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal beside the bathrooms\n🫎 I'll be 
 wearing my Moose Hat\n⏰ Meetup Time: 6:30 PM\n🚢 Ferry Departure: 6:45
  PM (Hanlan's Point Ferry)\nPLEASE BE ON TIME.\n🚢 Ferry Return: 9:45 PM
 \nOnce we're on the ferry\, it will be very difficult to catch up with the
  group.\n🎟️ Ferry Ticket: (Insert Current Fare)\n\nYou must purchase 
 your ticket before arriving.\n[CLICK HERE FOR TICKETS!](https://secure.tor
 onto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.jsp)\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fee
 : $5 cash in person or e-transfer to\n📧 [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mai
 lto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)\n\nThis fee helps support the group and all
 ows us to continue hosting events like this. Thank you for supporting comm
 unity! 💖\n\n***\n\n🎒 What to Bring\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable wal
 king shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 Light sweater or jacket\n🕶️ Sunglasses
 \n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n🌅 A sense of adventure\n\n***\n\n
 🌈 Who Is This For?\nThis group is open to anyone who wants to be social
  and make friends — whether single or not.\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n
 🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gather
 ings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welco
 me to just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nAnd a
 s always\, sometimes plans shift and events may need to be cancelled — p
 lease keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 Organizer: Mathew\nQuestions?
  Post on the event wall or email\n📧 [torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.co
 m](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)\nCome for the sunset.\nStay
  for the skyline.\nLeave feeling like you spent the evening somewhere far 
 away from the city — even though it was right beside it. 🌅✨
